complete -c netop -n '__fish_seen_subcommand_from traffic' -a pull -d 'Merge a pollers readings into this install. --remote fetches them over SSH; --file merges an export the poller wrote, which is what to use where SSH between the two subnets is not permitted -- an export is a file, and anything that can move a file will do. - reads standard input. A file is merged whole rather than by window, and merging is idempotent, so re-reading one adds nothing. Without --since a fetch resumes from the newest reading already merged, so a repeated pull carries only what is new.'
